 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "A card is a string: rank (\"2\"..\"10\", \"J\", \"Q\", \"K\", \"A\") followed by a suit letter S, H, D or C; cards in the deck are distinct. Same deal and output as level 1, with three-card poker categories from strongest: straight flush, three of a kind, straight, flush, pair, high card. A straight is three consecutive ranks with the ace high only (Q-K-A is a straight, A-2-3 is not); a flush is three cards of one suit. Straights, flushes and high cards compare all ranks from highest to lowest; three of a kind and pairs as in level 1. Return [hand1, hand2, winner] with winner 1, 2 or 0.",
  "provenance": [
